<title>ISRAEL: Israel's Discount Investments Q1 net up.</title>
<headline>Israel's Discount Investments Q1 net up.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Discount Investments Ltd reported the following first-quarter results:</p>
<p>			   (in thousands of shekels except per share)</p>
<p>			   Q1 97	Q1 96</p>
<p>Revenue		  93,039    79,621</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit	 73,581    57,647</p>
<p>Net profit	     66,783    55,226</p>
<p>Earnings per share    7.10	 5.90</p>
<p>Discount, a holding company, said a major contributor to its higher profits was Cellcom, a cellular phone operator, which reported profits of 87 million shekels in Q1 1997 against eight million shekels a year earlier.</p>
<p>Cellcom is owned by Bellsouth Corp, Brazil's Safra banking family and Discount Investment. It began operations two and a half years ago and has 675,000 subscribers.</p>
<p>($1=3.39 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
